// The standard library's own tests, written in Wip. The library is
// installed with the compiler, so its tests cannot live beside it, in
// `std/`, without being installed with every compiler: they live here, in a
// module of their own, and reach the library as a program does — through
// what it exports.
//
// `wip test tests/std/main.wip` runs them, and the gate does that too,
// debug and release, in `tests/gate/library`.
// The file itself holds nothing: the tests are in the `.test.wip` files
// beside it.
